# Hernan Cortes: the King's transport offer as in map_treasure_king_transport, but @KINGGALLEON3 ("for no extra charge": the Crown
# takes only the tax rate, 26%, not max((difficulty+10)*5, 2*tax) = 70%), and it is made although France owns a Galleon
# (FUN_465b_0000 waives the Galleon test for Cortes, FUN_281f_07b4(nation,10); FUN_5fef_1908 picks the text and the share by Cortes).
# Fixture (that test's, plus): Hernan Cortes in France's Congress (nation founding_fathers bit 10 + head.founding_father[10]);
# ship #2 (was a Caravel at sea (47,29)) is an empty Galleon, so France owns one; Treasure #131 (1000 gold) on (44,24) selected,
# Treasure #95 (500 gold) on (44,23). The offer text is longer than the non-Cortes one: its answer rows are at y 142 and 154.
key KP_6                   # east into Quebec: @KINGGALLEON3 offer popup
wait 2
click 160 136              # accept: Crown share 26% of 1000 = 260, 740 added (gold 429 -> 1169)
wait 2                    # @LOOTCASH popup
key Return
wait 3                    # the delete steps the active index back one record (FUN_1427_0824 raw 7834-7836); that sentried
                           # unit fails the re-test, so the cycle goes on from the treasure's slot: the units in Quebec first
key w                      # skip #136
key w                      # skip #144
key w                      # skip #147; the cycle wraps to the Colonist #88 riding the Caravel at sea
key s                    # sentry it (the hand-off used to skip it, port_bugs.md #1175a); Treasure #95 is selected
wait 1
key KP_3                   # SE into Quebec: offered again although France owns a Galleon
wait 2
click 165 148              # decline: the treasure stays in Quebec
wait 3                    # (no moves left; selection moves on to the ship #126 in Quebec, not past it)
